# Public keys that may sign a plugin's entitlements (ssh-keygen allowed_signers format):
#   stromy-entitlements namespaces="stromy-entitlements" ssh-ed25519 AAAA...
#
stromy-entitlements namespaces="stromy-entitlements" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIKrqsfAIDSaIsY6sEmyzoB062wDZkZoJDezbdIoB4rE3 stromy-entitlements 2026-10
# EMPTY ON PURPOSE until activation (ORG-PLAN-413 B3PA): the production key is minted by the
# operator, its PUBLIC half is added here as the only line, and its private half lives only in
# the `ENTITLEMENTS_SIGNING_KEY` secret of the private stromy-org repo. While this file holds no
# key line, the verifier fails every run ("verifier unavailable") - it can never pass.
#
# Rotation is add-then-remove: add the new public key as a second line and merge; switch the
# secret and re-sign every plugin; only then delete the old line.
